  "newPlayModeCases": 4,
  "newCoverage": [
    "Three consecutive genuine missing-target-path failures, each with an actionable bound retry menu; repeated clicks/old command calls/API calls do not produce parallel sessions.",
    "Old SceneLease objects reach terminal state, old batch handles invalidate, old IResourceManager cache and IEntityManager counts return to zero, and old HUD event channels shut down before the new session.",
    "After the test configuration restores the original target path, the retry button reaches Play with fresh Failure state, normal time scale, expected native scenes/actors and exactly one HUD subscription.",
    "The normal pause menu shows Resume and hides/disables Retry; direct Retry cannot restart normal Play.",
    "A selected real DefaultEntityHelper.CreateEntity failure retries successfully through the bound menu into a fresh normal helper/session.",
    "Explicit Exit and Bootstrap destruction cancel a pending retry while production cleanup still completes."
  ],
  "testBoundary": "Actual Unity, original scenes/assets and real Framework resource/UI/scene/entity/event managers. Missing-resource cases alter only a cloned SliceContent path; no asset file is deleted, substituted or mocked. Actor injection decorates DefaultEntityHelper at the selected failure site.",
  "resourceLifecycleBoundary": "EditorSimulation exercises native scenes, real AssetBatch handle invalidation, Framework cache clearing and module shutdown. Its asset loader does not provide production AssetBundle IO/reference-count behavior; no claim of Player/bundle lifecycle acceptance is made.",
